{
  "v": 1,
  "templates": [
    {
      "id": "haltech_cruise",
      "name": "Haltech cruise buttons",
      "maker": "Haltech",
      "pretends": "Haltech IO 12 Expander",
      "blurb": "Cruise control buttons on the screen. The ECU reads them as one analog input with a different voltage per button, plus an on/off switch.",
      "variants": [
        { "key": "A", "name": "IO Box A", "id_offset": 0 },
        { "key": "B", "name": "IO Box B", "id_offset": 1 }
      ],
      "device": {
        "id": "cruise_{v}",
        "name": "Cruise buttons, Box {V}",
        "template": "haltech_cruise",
        "bitrate": 1000,
        "controls": [
          { "id": "cruise", "name": "Cruise buttons", "kind": "select",
            "states": ["idle", "set", "resume", "cancel"] },
          { "id": "cruise_on", "name": "Cruise on/off", "kind": "latch" }
        ],
        "send": [
          { "can_id": 704, "dlc": 8, "every_ms": 20, "fields": [
            { "bit_start": 0, "bit_length": 16, "endian": 0, "scale": 0.001221001, "min": 0, "max": 5, "unit": "V",
              "control": "cruise", "values": [0, 5, 2.5, 4.29] }
          ] },
          { "can_id": 706, "dlc": 8, "every_ms": 20, "fields": [
            { "bit_start": 0, "bit_length": 8, "endian": 0, "control": "cruise_on", "values": [0, 250] }
          ] },
          { "can_id": 708, "dlc": 8, "every_ms": 20 },
          { "can_id": 710, "dlc": 5, "every_ms": 100, "data": "10090D0100" }
        ],
        "listen": [
          { "can_id": 720, "channels": [
            { "name": "IO{V}_DPO1", "bit_start": 0, "bit_length": 8, "endian": 0, "scale": 0.4, "unit": "%" },
            { "name": "IO{V}_DPO2", "bit_start": 32, "bit_length": 8, "endian": 0, "scale": 0.4, "unit": "%" }
          ] }
        ]
      },
      "labels": {
        "704": "Analog inputs 1-4",
        "706": "Switch inputs 1-2",
        "708": "Switch inputs 3-4",
        "710": "Keep-alive",
        "720": "Outputs 1-2 from the ECU"
      },
      "guide": [
        "In NSP, open the IO 12 Expander and tick Box {V}.",
        "Set Analog Input 1 to Cruise Control multi-button. Set Switch Input 1 to Cruise Control enable.",
        "For each button: hold it on the dash, and while holding it click Calibrate for that function in NSP.",
        "Cruise control also needs drive-by-wire and a vehicle speed input set up, and a clutch switch on a manual.",
        "Optional: set Output 1 to the cruise active lamp. The dash shows it as channel IO{V}_DPO1."
      ]
    },
    {
